<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jammu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jammu is a city on the Tawi river in the foothills of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalaya</a>, the winter capital of the Indian union territory of Jammu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>, and the name of the surrounding region. It was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dogras">Dogra</a> Rajas, who under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> absorbed the neighbouring hill states and in 1846 became rulers of the princely state of Jammu and Kashmir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jammu.jpg" alt="Jammu" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Imviiku · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hari_niwas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the Punjab riots between 200,000 and 2,000,000 people were killed; some 6.5 million Muslims moved to West Pakistan and 4.7 million Hindus and Sikhs to India, the largest migration in human history, and a dispute over <b>Jammu</b> and Kashmir brought war with India in 1947–1948.</blockquote><a href="/empire/islamic-republic-of-pakistan">Islamic Republic of Pakistan · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Since 2014 Modi's governments have introduced a national goods and services tax, revoked the special status of <b>Jammu</b> and Kashmir in 2019 and invested heavily in infrastructure, while critics point to pressure on minorities, the press and institutions.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-india">Republic of India · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>On 5 August 2019 the Modi administration revoked the limited autonomy of <b>Jammu</b> and Kashmir under Article 370, a decision upheld by the Supreme Court; it was accompanied by the deployment of thousands of security forces, the detention of Kashmiri politicians and thousands of civilians, and a years-long…</blockquote><a href="/ideology/hindutva">Hindutva · In Power</a></li><li><blockquote>Politically, Basohli was a minor state between Chamba and <b>Jammu</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/basohli-state">Basohli State</a></li><li><blockquote>It lay on the Tawi river on the route from <b>Jammu</b> towards Kashmir.</blockquote><a href="/state/chenani-state">Chenani State</a></li><li><blockquote>Gulab Singh, a Dogra noble who had served Ranjit Singh and became Raja of <b>Jammu</b>, extended his rule to Ladakh.</blockquote><a href="/state/jammu-and-kashmir-princely-state">Jammu and Kashmir (princely state)</a></li></ul></section>
